<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">tutorial</ansi>

New characters begin in a short course of rooms, their own copy of it, that
teaches the basics one lesson at a time. The way into each next room opens
when you have done what the lesson asks:

  <ansi fg="yellow">Character</ansi>  look yourself over: status, inventory, experience, conditions.
  <ansi fg="yellow">Company</ansi>    recruit two companions.
  <ansi fg="yellow">Formation</ansi>  put one in the front row and another behind.
  <ansi fg="yellow">Survival</ansi>   eat and drink, and check the weather, temperature, strain,
             and cargo. The wardens hand you food or water if you have none.
  <ansi fg="yellow">Camp</ansi>       make camp, light a fire, and rest until you are Rested.
  <ansi fg="yellow">Departure</ansi>  walk out through the gate.
Your place in the course is saved,
so logging out and back in picks up where you left off.

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage: </ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">tutorial</ansi>
  Show the current lesson, its goal, a checklist, and hints.

  <ansi fg="command">tutorial next</ansi>
  Move past a lesson you cannot finish, for example when both tutorial
  recruits were already claimed by an earlier character on your account,
  when you have nothing left to eat or drink (the meal is waived, the
  checks aren't), or when camping isn't available.

  <ansi fg="command">tutorial skip</ansi>
  Leave the course now, for the town. It asks you to confirm with
  <ansi fg="command">tutorial skip yes</ansi>. Skipping gives no graduation reward.

Every command works during the course: chat, <ansi fg="command">help</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">status</ansi>, and the rest.
Once you have left the course, it is finished and can't be restarted.
